g for the full  liability  in the year in which their accrued  allowing your capital assets to fall  into disrepair using your remaining  assets to borrow more without a public  vote all the attributes of an  institution that does not have fiscal  health they've had a culture develop at  City Hall that doesn't treat residents  as customers and shareholders but rather  as a nuisance if you will they have a  culture at City Hall that we shouldn't  promote small businesses that small  businesses basically our ATM machines go  hit them up for a higher tax or a higher  fee don't mention the fact that 80 80  percent of our roads are deemed in  unacceptable condition forget the fact  that we have a billion dollars in  deferred maintenance debt at least if  not more forget the fact that we're  raising taxes and fees forget the fact  that services are at the lowest level  we've ever seen by golly we need a  brand-new million square foot half a  billion dollar City Hall oh by the way  did I mention we're in the biggest  commercial real estate bubble that we've  ever seen it's completely crashed we  have twenty four percent vacancy in  downtown commercial real estate and yet  city government is about to add a  million square feet of additional  inventory this is almost like the  captain of the Titanic announcing a  dinner party as the ship is going down  the city's operating deficit has a  number of angles to it the city has  rated its infrastructure accounts so  there's a deferred maintenance deficit  even if it's not on the balance sheet if  you let your streets your sidewalks your  public facilities fall into disrepair  because you're not providing for the  basic maintenance the annual operations  and maintenance costs you will have a  capital liability grow our deferred  maintenance deficit debt right now is a  1 billion dollars second we face a  pension deficit debt of two billion  dollars in climbing primarily driven by  unsustainable benefits third we face a  one point 